  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 228 AM MST Mon Nov 23 2026\n\nActive week ahead but not particularly impactful. We have a \nshortwave trough passing through the region today. We may see \nsome pockets of light snow, mainly across the mountains and \nhighlands. Amounts look light and not much more than a dusting. \nOur next system arrives Thursday into Friday. However, this is a\nnorthwest flow system and the central mountains tend to shadow \nmuch of the east Idaho in these situations. So most of the snow \nwill fall north of Ketchum and across the eastern highlands. \nSnow levels with this system will likely be above 6500 feet and \namounts look light with a couple inches possible. Potentially we\ncould see better chances for widespread precipitation later in \nthe weekend into early next week as a low pressure system moves \ninto the Pacific Northwest with rain/snow possible for the \nvalleys. Temperatures are expected to be relatively seasonable \nthis week.",
